# Model, messages, and the overlay view

Everything built in the first three parts meets inside the Foldkit application — the shared vocabulary of the promontory, the deterministic generator, the HTTP endpoints, and the Three.js scene controller. Here the visitor's intent, the server-rendered HTML document, and the WebGL canvas become a single state machine.

Foldkit brings The Elm Architecture to Effect. `Flags` carry the initial `TownSnapshot` from the server into the browser without re-running generation on hydration. `Model` holds the complete state of the page in one `Schema.Struct`. `Message` enumerates every event that can happen in the application as a past-tense fact. `update` is a pure, exhaustive function from a `Model` and a `Message` to the next `Model` and a list of declarative `Command` values. `Mount` and `Subscription` bridge ongoing streams such as the Three.js canvas lifecycle and the solar cycle timer back into messages, while `view` renders the `Model` into an SSR-compatible HTML document whose translucent panels float over the promontory.

## Flags, Model, and the scene projection

When the server renders the page, it resolves a `TownSnapshot` and serializes it into the HTML document as the application's `Flags`. On hydration, the browser decodes those same `Flags` and calls `init` to produce the initial `Model`.

The `Model` extends the snapshot's fields with interactive UI state that exists only while a visitor explores the town: which district card is focused (`selectedDistrict`), whether a new seed request is in flight (`isGeneratingTown`), the most recent bell chime report (`lastBellChime`), whether the HUD panels are collapsed (`hudCollapsed`), and whether the WebGL canvas has finished mounting (`canvasMounted`).

Because the Three.js viewport only reads the ten visual parameters of `TownSceneState`, `toSceneState` projects the full `Model` down to that narrower contract whenever a transition synchronizes the 3D scene.

=>

export const Flags = TownSnapshot
export type Flags = typeof Flags.Type

export const Model = Schema.Struct({
  townName: Schema.String,
  region: Schema.String,
  seed: Schema.Number,
  timeOfDay: TimeOfDay,
  palette: TownPalette,
  cameraPreset: CameraPreset,
  sunAngle: Schema.Number,
  windBreeze: Schema.Number,
  autoOrbit: Schema.Boolean,
  autoTimeCycle: Schema.Boolean,
  lanternsLit: Schema.Boolean,
  bellsRinging: Schema.Boolean,
  population: Schema.Number,
  activeBoats: Schema.Number,
  harborTempC: Schema.Number,
  seaState: Schema.String,
  districts: Schema.Array(DistrictInfo),
  selectedDistrict: Schema.Option(DistrictId),
  isGeneratingTown: Schema.Boolean,
  lastBellChime: Schema.Option(BellChimeResponse),
  hudCollapsed: Schema.Boolean,
  renderedAt: Schema.String,
  renderedOn: Schema.Literals(['Server', 'Client']),
  canvasMounted: Schema.Boolean,
})
export type Model = typeof Model.Type

export const toSceneState = (model: Model): TownSceneState =>
  TownSceneState.make({
    seed: model.seed,
    timeOfDay: model.timeOfDay,
    palette: model.palette,
    cameraPreset: model.cameraPreset,
    sunAngle: model.sunAngle,
    windBreeze: model.windBreeze,
    autoOrbit: model.autoOrbit,
    lanternsLit: model.lanternsLit,
    bellsRinging: model.bellsRinging,
    selectedDistrict: model.selectedDistrict,
  })

## Past-tense messages

In Foldkit, messages are not imperative instructions ("select palette", "ring bells"); they are facts about what just happened (`SelectedPalette`, `ClickedRingCampanileBells`, `SucceededRingBells`). Naming every variant in the past tense keeps the boundary clear: views, commands, mounts, and subscriptions report events, and only `update` decides what those events mean.

=>

export const Message = defineMessageUnion({
  SelectedTimeOfDay: { timeOfDay: TimeOfDay },
  SelectedPalette: { palette: TownPalette },
  SelectedCameraPreset: { cameraPreset: CameraPreset },
  ChangedSunAngle: { sunAngle: Schema.Number },
  ChangedWindBreeze: { windBreeze: Schema.Number },
  ToggledAutoOrbit: {},
  ToggledAutoTimeCycle: {},
  ToggledLanterns: {},
  ToggledHudCollapsed: {},
  SelectedDistrictCard: { districtId: Schema.Option(DistrictId) },
  SelectedDistrictFromCanvas: { districtId: DistrictId },
  ClickedRegenerateTown: {},
  SucceededGenerateTown: { snapshot: TownSnapshot },
  FailedGenerateTown: { reason: Schema.String },
  ClickedRingCampanileBells: {},
  SucceededRingBells: { chime: BellChimeResponse },
  CompletedBellResonance: {},
  MountedTownCanvas: {},
  CompletedSyncScene: {},
  CompletedPersistCookie: {},
  TickedAutoCycle: {},
})
export type Message = typeof Message.Type

## Declarative commands

`update` never performs side effects in place. When a transition needs to push state into the Three.js controller, write the visitor's cookie, ask the backend for a new seed, or ring the campanile bells, it returns a `Command` value alongside the new `Model`.

Two local commands synchronize browser state. `SyncTownScene` reads `getActiveTownController`, which returns an `Option.Option<IsometricTownController>`, and maps `controller.applyState(sceneState)` over it when the canvas is mounted. `PersistTownPreferences` writes the `{ seed, palette, timeOfDay }` JSON payload into the `borgo_solare_prefs` cookie so the next server render starts from the visitor's chosen atmosphere.

=>

export const SyncTownScene = Command.define('SyncTownScene', {
  args: { sceneState: TownSceneState },
  messages: [Message.CompletedSyncScene],
  execute: ({ sceneState }) =>
    Effect.sync(() => {
      Option.map(getActiveTownController(), (controller) => {
        controller.applyState(sceneState)
      })
      return Message.CompletedSyncScene()
    }),
})

export const PersistTownPreferences = Command.define('PersistTownPreferences', {
  args: {
    seed: Schema.Number,
    palette: TownPalette,
    timeOfDay: TimeOfDay,
  },
  messages: [Message.CompletedPersistCookie],
  execute: ({ seed, palette, timeOfDay }) =>
    Effect.sync(() => {
      const payload = encodeURIComponent(
        JSON.stringify({ seed, palette, timeOfDay }),
      )
      document.cookie = `${TOWN_COOKIE_NAME}=${payload}; path=/; max-age=31536000; samesite=lax`
      return Message.CompletedPersistCookie()
    }),
})

~

Two network commands talk to the Effect backend and fall back cleanly when the site is hosted on a static CDN such as GitHub Pages. `RequestNewTownFromBackend` posts `{ palette, timeOfDay }` to `/api/town/generate` and decodes the response through `TownSnapshot`; if the server is unreachable, it synthesizes a fresh snapshot locally via `createTownSnapshot` so the button works identically in static builds. `TriggerCampanileBells` triggers the Web Audio chime and 3D seagull burst on the active controller, then posts `{ seed }` to `/api/town/bells` for acoustic telemetry, falling back to a default `Campana Maggiore` reading when offline. `ExpireBellResonance` sleeps for 3,800 milliseconds and emits `CompletedBellResonance` so the bell-ringing state settles automatically.

=>

class TownApiError extends Data.TaggedError('TownApiError')<{
  readonly reason: string
}> {}

const decodeSnapshotEffect = Schema.decodeUnknownEffect(TownSnapshot)
const decodeBellChimeEffect = Schema.decodeUnknownEffect(BellChimeResponse)

export const RequestNewTownFromBackend = Command.define(
  'RequestNewTownFromBackend',
  {
    args: {
      palette: TownPalette,
      timeOfDay: TimeOfDay,
    },
    messages: [Message.SucceededGenerateTown, Message.FailedGenerateTown],
    execute: ({ palette, timeOfDay }) =>
      Effect.gen(function* () {
        const response = yield* Effect.tryPromise({
          try: () =>
            fetch('/api/town/generate', {
              method: 'POST',
              headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },
              body: JSON.stringify({ palette, timeOfDay }),
            }),
          catch: () =>
            new TownApiError({ reason: 'Network request failed' }),
        })

        if (!response.ok) {
          return yield* new TownApiError({ reason: 'Static host fallback' })
        }

        const json = yield* Effect.tryPromise({
          try: () => response.json(),
          catch: () =>
            new TownApiError({ reason: 'Invalid JSON from Effect backend' }),
        })

        const snapshot = yield* decodeSnapshotEffect(json).pipe(
          Effect.mapError(
            () =>
              new TownApiError({
                reason: 'Schema validation failed for TownSnapshot',
              }),
          ),
        )

        return Message.SucceededGenerateTown({ snapshot })
      }).pipe(
        Effect.catch(() =>
          Effect.sync(() => {
            const nextSeed = Math.floor(100 + Math.random() * 8900)
            const snapshot = createTownSnapshot({
              seed: nextSeed,
              palette,
              timeOfDay,
              renderedOn: 'Client',
            })
            return Message.SucceededGenerateTown({ snapshot })
          }),
        ),
      ),
  },
)

export const TriggerCampanileBells = Command.define('TriggerCampanileBells', {
  args: { seed: Schema.Number },
  messages: [Message.SucceededRingBells],
  execute: ({ seed }) =>
    Effect.gen(function* () {
      Option.map(getActiveTownController(), (controller) => {
        controller.triggerBellChime()
      })

      const response = yield* Effect.tryPromise({
        try: () =>
          fetch('/api/town/bells', {
            method: 'POST',
            headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' },
            body: JSON.stringify({ seed }),
          }),
        catch: () =>
          new TownApiError({ reason: 'Bell endpoint unreachable' }),
      })

      if (!response.ok) {
        return yield* new TownApiError({ reason: 'Bell endpoint status error' })
      }

      const raw = yield* Effect.tryPromise({
        try: () => response.json(),
        catch: () => new TownApiError({ reason: 'Invalid bell JSON' }),
      })

      const chime = yield* decodeBellChimeEffect(raw)
      return Message.SucceededRingBells({ chime })
    }).pipe(
      Effect.catch(() =>
        Effect.succeed(
          Message.SucceededRingBells({
            chime: BellChimeResponse.make({
              chimeNote: 'D♯4 · Campana Maggiore',
              seagullsStartled: 8,
              echoDurationMs: 3600,
              timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
            }),
          }),
        ),
      ),
    ),
})

export const ExpireBellResonance = Command.define('ExpireBellResonance', {
  messages: [Message.CompletedBellResonance],
  execute: Effect.sleep(Duration.millis(3800)).pipe(
    Effect.as(Message.CompletedBellResonance()),
  ),
})

## Mounting the canvas and subscribing to the solar cycle

The `#town-canvas-container` element hosts the Three.js renderer. Foldkit's `Mount.defineStream` gives that DOM node a scoped Effect lifecycle. `Effect.acquireRelease` mounts the isometric town on the element and guarantees `instance.dispose()` runs if the element ever unmounts. Raycast clicks on 3D district hitboxes are offered into the stream's queue as `SelectedDistrictFromCanvas` messages, while `viewStateChanges` pauses the animation loop whenever the document is hidden. Once mounted, the stream emits `MountedTownCanvas` and stays open with `Effect.never` for the lifetime of the scope.

Alongside the mount, `subscriptions` defines `autoCycle`: whenever `model.autoTimeCycle` is `true`, a 220-millisecond `Stream.tick` emits `TickedAutoCycle` messages to advance the sun across the sky.

=>

export const MountTownViewport = Mount.defineStream('MountTownViewport', {
  args: { initialScene: TownSceneState },
  messages: [
    Message.MountedTownCanvas,
    Message.SelectedDistrictFromCanvas,
  ],
  execute: ({ element, viewStateChanges, initialScene }) =>
    Stream.callback<
      | typeof Message.MountedTownCanvas.Type
      | typeof Message.SelectedDistrictFromCanvas.Type
    >((queue) =>
      Effect.gen(function* () {
        const controller = yield* Effect.acquireRelease(
          Effect.sync(() =>
            mountIsometricTown(element, initialScene, (districtId) => {
              Queue.offerUnsafe(
                queue,
                Message.SelectedDistrictFromCanvas({ districtId }),
              )
            }),
          ),
          (instance) => Effect.sync(() => instance.dispose()),
        )

        yield* viewStateChanges.pipe(
          Stream.runForEach((viewState) =>
            Effect.sync(() => controller.setPaused(viewState !== 'Live')),
          ),
          Effect.forkScoped,
        )

        Queue.offerUnsafe(queue, Message.MountedTownCanvas())
        return yield* Effect.never
      }),
    ),
})

export const subscriptions = Subscription.make<Model, Message>()((entry) => ({
  autoCycle: entry(
    { autoTimeCycle: Schema.Boolean },
    {
      modelToDependencies: (model) => ({
        autoTimeCycle: model.autoTimeCycle,
      }),
      dependenciesToStream: ({ autoTimeCycle }) =>
        Stream.when(
          Stream.tick(Duration.millis(220)).pipe(
            Stream.drop(1),
            Stream.map(() => Message.TickedAutoCycle()),
          ),
          Effect.sync(() => autoTimeCycle),
        ),
    },
  ),
}))

## Initialization and the pure update transition

`init` turns `Flags` into the initial `Model`, starting with no district focused (`Option.none()`), no bell chime toast (`Option.none()`), the HUD panels expanded, and `canvasMounted` set to `false` until hydration completes on the client.

When the visitor drags the solar elevation slider or lets the solar cycle tick, `deriveTimeOfDayFromAngle` maps the continuous sun angle back onto one of the four canonical `TimeOfDay` phases using `Match.value`.

`update` then handles all twenty-one `Message` variants exhaustively via `Message.match`. Every branch updates the immutable `Model` with Foldkit's `modifyFields` and declares the exact commands that should run as a consequence.

=>

export const init: Runtime.ApplicationInit<Model, Message, Flags> = (flags) => ({
  model: Model.make({
    townName: flags.townName,
    region: flags.region,
    seed: flags.seed,
    timeOfDay: flags.timeOfDay,
    palette: flags.palette,
    cameraPreset: flags.cameraPreset,
    sunAngle: flags.sunAngle,
    windBreeze: flags.windBreeze,
    autoOrbit: flags.autoOrbit,
    autoTimeCycle: flags.autoTimeCycle,
    lanternsLit: flags.lanternsLit,
    bellsRinging: flags.bellsRinging,
    population: flags.population,
    activeBoats: flags.activeBoats,
    harborTempC: flags.harborTempC,
    seaState: flags.seaState,
    districts: flags.districts,
    selectedDistrict: Option.none(),
    isGeneratingTown: false,
    lastBellChime: Option.none(),
    hudCollapsed: false,
    renderedAt: flags.renderedAt,
    renderedOn: flags.renderedOn,
    canvasMounted: false,
  }),
})

const deriveTimeOfDayFromAngle = (angle: number): TimeOfDay =>
  Match.value(angle).pipe(
    Match.when(
      (a) => a < -6,
      () => 'Starlight' as const,
    ),
    Match.when(
      (a) => a < 20,
      () => 'GoldenHour' as const,
    ),
    Match.when(
      (a) => a < 38,
      () => 'Dawn' as const,
    ),
    Match.orElse(() => 'Midday' as const),
  )

export const update = (
  model: Model,
  message: Message,
): Update.Return<Model, Message> =>
  Message.match<Update.Return<Model, Message>>(message, {
    SelectedTimeOfDay: ({ timeOfDay }) => {
      const nextModel = modifyFields(model, {
        timeOfDay: () => timeOfDay,
        sunAngle: () => defaultSunAngleForTime(timeOfDay),
        lanternsLit: () => defaultLanternsForTime(timeOfDay),
      })
      return {
        model: nextModel,
        commands: [
          SyncTownScene({ sceneState: toSceneState(nextModel) }),
          PersistTownPreferences({
            seed: nextModel.seed,
            palette: nextModel.palette,
            timeOfDay: nextModel.timeOfDay,
          }),
        ],
      }
    },

    SelectedPalette: ({ palette }) => {
      const nextModel = modifyFields(model, {
        palette: () => palette,
      })
      return {
        model: nextModel,
        commands: [
          SyncTownScene({ sceneState: toSceneState(nextModel) }),
          PersistTownPreferences({
            seed: nextModel.seed,
            palette: nextModel.palette,
            timeOfDay: nextModel.timeOfDay,
          }),
        ],
      }
    },

    SelectedCameraPreset: ({ cameraPreset }) => {
      const nextModel = modifyFields(model, {
        cameraPreset: () => cameraPreset,
        selectedDistrict: () => Option.none(),
      })
      return {
        model: nextModel,
        commands: [SyncTownScene({ sceneState: toSceneState(nextModel) })],
      }
    },

    ChangedSunAngle: ({ sunAngle }) => {
      const clamped = Math.max(-35, Math.min(85, sunAngle))
      const derivedTime = deriveTimeOfDayFromAngle(clamped)
      const nextModel = modifyFields(model, {
        sunAngle: () => clamped,
        timeOfDay: () => derivedTime,
        lanternsLit: () => clamped < 24,
      })
      return {
        model: nextModel,
        commands: [SyncTownScene({ sceneState: toSceneState(nextModel) })],
      }
    },

    ChangedWindBreeze: ({ windBreeze }) => {
      const clamped = Math.max(0.2, Math.min(2.5, windBreeze))
      const nextModel = modifyFields(model, {
        windBreeze: () => clamped,
      })
      return {
        model: nextModel,
        commands: [SyncTownScene({ sceneState: toSceneState(nextModel) })],
      }
    },

    ToggledAutoOrbit: () => {
      const nextModel = modifyFields(model, {
        autoOrbit: (current) => !current,
      })
      return {
        model: nextModel,
        commands: [SyncTownScene({ sceneState: toSceneState(nextModel) })],
      }
    },

    ToggledAutoTimeCycle: () => ({
      model: modifyFields(model, {
        autoTimeCycle: (current) => !current,
      }),
    }),

    ToggledLanterns: () => {
      const nextModel = modifyFields(model, {
        lanternsLit: (current) => !current,
      })
      return {
        model: nextModel,
        commands: [SyncTownScene({ sceneState: toSceneState(nextModel) })],
      }
    },

    ToggledHudCollapsed: () => ({
      model: modifyFields(model, {
        hudCollapsed: (current) => !current,
      }),
    }),

    SelectedDistrictCard: ({ districtId }) => {
      const nextModel = modifyFields(model, {
        selectedDistrict: () => districtId,
      })
      return {
        model: nextModel,
        commands: [SyncTownScene({ sceneState: toSceneState(nextModel) })],
      }
    },

    SelectedDistrictFromCanvas: ({ districtId }) => {
      const nextSelected = Option.contains(model.selectedDistrict, districtId)
        ? Option.none<DistrictId>()
        : Option.some(districtId)

      const nextModel = modifyFields(model, {
        selectedDistrict: () => nextSelected,
      })
      return {
        model: nextModel,
        commands: [SyncTownScene({ sceneState: toSceneState(nextModel) })],
      }
    },

    ClickedRegenerateTown: () => ({
      model: modifyFields(model, {
        isGeneratingTown: () => true,
      }),
      commands: [
        RequestNewTownFromBackend({
          palette: model.palette,
          timeOfDay: model.timeOfDay,
        }),
      ],
    }),

    SucceededGenerateTown: ({ snapshot }) => {
      const nextModel = modifyFields(model, {
        townName: () => snapshot.townName,
        region: () => snapshot.region,
        seed: () => snapshot.seed,
        population: () => snapshot.population,
        activeBoats: () => snapshot.activeBoats,
        harborTempC: () => snapshot.harborTempC,
        seaState: () => snapshot.seaState,
        districts: () => snapshot.districts,
        renderedAt: () => snapshot.renderedAt,
        isGeneratingTown: () => false,
        selectedDistrict: () => Option.none(),
      })
      return {
        model: nextModel,
        commands: [SyncTownScene({ sceneState: toSceneState(nextModel) })],
      }
    },

    FailedGenerateTown: () => {
      const fallbackSeed =
        (((model.seed * 1664525 + 1013904223) >>> 0) % 8900) + 100
      const nextModel = modifyFields(model, {
        seed: () => fallbackSeed,
        isGeneratingTown: () => false,
      })
      return {
        model: nextModel,
        commands: [SyncTownScene({ sceneState: toSceneState(nextModel) })],
      }
    },

    ClickedRingCampanileBells: () => {
      const nextModel = modifyFields(model, {
        bellsRinging: () => true,
        selectedDistrict: () => Option.some('duomo' as const),
      })
      return {
        model: nextModel,
        commands: [
          SyncTownScene({ sceneState: toSceneState(nextModel) }),
          TriggerCampanileBells({ seed: nextModel.seed }),
          ExpireBellResonance(),
        ],
      }
    },

    SucceededRingBells: ({ chime }) => ({
      model: modifyFields(model, {
        lastBellChime: () => Option.some(chime),
      }),
    }),

    CompletedBellResonance: () => {
      const nextModel = modifyFields(model, {
        bellsRinging: () => false,
      })
      return {
        model: nextModel,
        commands: [SyncTownScene({ sceneState: toSceneState(nextModel) })],
      }
    },

    MountedTownCanvas: () => {
      const nextModel = modifyFields(model, {
        canvasMounted: () => true,
      })
      return {
        model: nextModel,
        commands: [SyncTownScene({ sceneState: toSceneState(nextModel) })],
      }
    },

    CompletedSyncScene: () => ({ model }),

    CompletedPersistCookie: () => ({ model }),

    TickedAutoCycle: () => {
      const nextSun =
        model.sunAngle >= 80
          ? -32
          : Math.round((model.sunAngle + 1.5) * 10) / 10
      const nextTime = deriveTimeOfDayFromAngle(nextSun)
      const nextModel = modifyFields(model, {
        sunAngle: () => nextSun,
        timeOfDay: () => nextTime,
        lanternsLit: () => nextSun < 24,
      })
      return {
        model: nextModel,
        commands: [SyncTownScene({ sceneState: toSceneState(nextModel) })],
      }
    },
  })

## The architectural HUD overlay view

The view layer renders a full-screen layout with `#town-canvas-container` behind a translucent `pointer-events-none` HUD overlay. `pointer-events-auto` is enabled only on the interactive cards and buttons so mouse drags on open space pass straight through to the Three.js orbit controls.

Three sub-views compose the HUD. `renderTopHeader` displays the town's generated name, the SSR provenance badge, the active seed, the region and palette subtitle, and the action buttons for ringing the Duomo bells, requesting a new seed from the Effect backend, or collapsing the side panels. `renderLeftControlsPanel` houses the four `TimeOfDay` buttons, the solar elevation and Maestrale breeze range inputs, the four regional stucco and majolica palette cards with color swatches, the four camera viewpoint presets, and the simulation toggles. `renderRightDistrictsPanel` displays the live telemetry counters, an optional bell-chime toast rendered via `Option.match(model.lastBellChime, ...)`, and the list of five `Quartieri del Borgo` cards that synchronize bidirectionally with 3D raycast selection.

=>

const TIME_OPTIONS: ReadonlyArray<
  Readonly<{ id: TimeOfDay; short: string; badge: string }>
> = [
  { id: 'Dawn', short: 'Alba', badge: '06:15' },
